    "result_text": "The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe locality derivation now prefers the postcode, falling back to the city-to-region table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`CityRegion.java`** \u2014 Added an overload `localityOf(String city, String postcode)` that:\n   - Looks up the region whose postcode range contains the postcode first (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099).\n   - Falls back to the existing city-to-region lookup when the postcode is absent, non-numeric, or in no known range.\n   - Returns `\"UNKNOWN\"` when neither yields a region.\n   \n   The original single-arg `localityOf(city)` and `postcodeRangeOf(city)` are unchanged, so postcode *validation* still keys off the city as before.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 The `locality` mapping now passes `owner.getPostcode()` alongside the city.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Updated the `locality` field description to document postcode-first derivation.\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. Both `coreRegionFromPostcodeRange` (Sydney/2000 \u2192 NSW, still same region for known cities) and `functionalityPostcodePreferredOverCity` (unknown city + 3000 \u2192 VIC, disambiguating via postcode) pass.",
